WEBVTT

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:04.830
"What's that racket?"

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.950
"And I thought I was beating, that bucket of bolts is gaining on me!"

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:24.000
"Away from this lunatic, he's gonna kill someone!"

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.190
Another Formula 1 race driver bites the dust.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:17.030
You're not very good for a formula driver.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.930
How did you know that? Who are you?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.320
I'm known as the Silver Phantom. Heard of me, no doubt.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.420
I've heard of you. You're the madman who's been knocking off veteran drivers.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.860
Nice being famous.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.450
but that's nothing compared to the fame I'll have after CRUSHING the Mach 5!

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.200
What? Mach 5?

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:40.150
Yeah, the Mach 5 and Speed Racer.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:44.210
I'll soon find them both and destroy them!

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:06.870
Hey Sparky, good morning.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.940
Well, well, hello there Speed, what's going on?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.460
Yo pal, you look exhausted.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:20.030
I don't know, I was so revved up after yesterday's race that I just couldn't get to sleep.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.910
And when I finally did, I was having all these wild dreams.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:27.110
Wild dreams, do tell, what's that all about?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.000
I dreamt I saw my brother Rex.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.580
that I was racing in his car.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.380
It seemed like he was alive again.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:46.240
Oh, my... Here's your coffee, dear.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:47.700
Thanks there, sweetie.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.420
This coffee's gonna hit the spot.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.210
Listen, I peeked into Speed's room

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.630
and he's not there. Have you seen him?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.900
Well, he came home last night. Maybe he's out

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.000
jogging. Out jogging? After

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.900
yesterday's race somehow I doubt that he was exhausted well you gotta understand

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.620
car racing energizes you I mean it's amazing he even got to sleep must have

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:13.940
bolted up after an hour in bed well that doesn't make me feel any better still

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:18.550
into racing even after what happened to his dear dear brother you'd think speed

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:22.670
would forget about cars after Rex's death I don't want to lose two sons to

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:30.000
this awful sport I know it still hurts speed races because he has to just like his brother

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.310
Rex had to race. Racing is part of Speed's heritage. It's in his bones. You can take

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:43.070
the boy out of the car, but you can't take the car. Speak of the devil. Speed, where

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:50.900
were you? I was worried. Well, I went out for a little run. See? I told you you had

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:54.870
nothing to worry about. Why do I get the feeling that you guys were talking about me?

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:00.000
Speed, to be honest with you, I'm a bit concerned about your racing. Concerned?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.760
about racing why mom i'm not a kid anymore mother's more concerned about your change of heart

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:11.670
for so long you hated the thought of racing and now it's all you think about oh i don't think i

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:21.000
ever hated racing what i hated is that it took rex's life when dad rebuilt the mach 5 my passion

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:29.030
came back my passion for racing then i remembered my promise your promise yeah

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.630
I promised Rex that I'd be a great racer.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:36.230
Speed, aim to become a superior racer. You must promise.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.460
Rex forced you into this promise?

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:42.790
Not force. An agreement.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:49.200
Oh, forgive me. You're a big boy now, and I'm sure that any decision you make will be the right one.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.600
So you have my blessing.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:55.130
Thanks, Mom. That means a lot to me.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:00.000
What are we getting so glum about? With Speed behind the wheel of the Mach 5, he'll be a success.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.210
safe as a baby in a crib. Right, kid?

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:05.570
And there's the Safety 7 that Pop's installed.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.940
Now you're talking.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:11.430
Look, I've got a little appointment, so if you'll excuse me...

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:16.580
Wait, Speed, I have something. Just a little something to take with you.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:21.350
Flowers? How'd you know I was going to the racetrack?

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:25.100
Leave them there for me, in Rex's memory.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.840
I will, Mom. You sure know how to read a guy's mind.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.960
That's one good kid.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:39.480
Now, uh, pardon me, but while we're on the subject of mind reading...

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.050
Yes, let me guess, my husband is starving for his breakfast, right?

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:47.120
That's two for two, mother!

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:50.480
You ought to take your act on the road!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:18.450
Trixie I got this brainstorm figured out how the famous speed can help the soon famous Trixie Fontaine

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:23.580
Just pull over speed will ya you gotta be nuts having a conversation on the highway

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:28.340
Well the only time you pay attention to anything is when it's wrapped in a car here

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:34.650
Nifty photos, huh? I'm pretty good with the camera, don't you think?

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.750
Is that why you pulled me over, Trixie?

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:43.080
Well, the photos are really hot, but I need something else.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.280
Like what?

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.150
Like a one-on-one interview with the up-and-coming Speed Racer.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.270
I mean, a little publicity never hurt anyone.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.290
Not to mention what it would do for my career in the media.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:56.450
Sounds great, but not right now. I gotta run.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.000
Wait a minute! Don't move, Speed! I'll be right with you!

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:01.870
Oh, brother.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:10.740
Miss, huh?

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.000
Fill her up, check the oil, wash it, and take your time.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.160
I'll be right back, hon.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.320
Uh, but...

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.220
Wait a minute.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:19.190
Thanks!

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.950
Wow! It's the Mach 5!

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:30.000
No getting rid?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.290
of you. Thanks, Speed. I knew you'd understand how important it was for me to get this interview,

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:39.320
what it would mean for my career to have an exclusive with Speed Racer. Well, I'll tell

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:48.370
you one thing. You're certainly persistent. You can be sure I ditch my car for a ride

00:09:48.370 --> 00:10:00.000
the Mach 5. You! Yes, sir. Can I help you? My goodness. Sorry, sir. Does the

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:07.600
Mach 5 frequent this place. Mach 5? Never seen it here before. But oh, that's some set of wheels.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:14.360
I would love to get under the hood of that thing and tinker with it. Listen, will the Mach 5 return?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:25.080
Answer! Huh? Chit chat, let's get started with this interview. Just say whatever comes to mind.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:30.000
Huh? What was it like the first time you saw the Mach 5? Do you mean the rebuilt?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.000
Mach 5?

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.000
Yes.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.110
The first time.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.110
It was quite an experience hard to forget.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:45.510
It was about a year ago that Pop showed me the secret garage beneath the Mach 5 compound.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:49.490
It was a strange, almost frightening place.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:53.240
After an endless flight of stairs, I arrived at an impressive doorway.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:10.760
this place this was once your brother's top-secret research center and now the

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:22.880
secret's out holy mackerel not a bad-looking dump huh

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:30.000
the mock five totally rebuilt tip-top shape if i say so myself

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:35.690
Re-equipped, titanium wheels, triple-alloy paint, the most advanced auto in the world.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:38.940
It's unbelievable. It's spectacular.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:43.640
I was going to keep it a secret from you, son, but now...

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:47.320
Well, with your brother Rex gone, I'm going to need a driver for this heap.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.850
It's hardly a heap, Dad.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.860
With Sparky's help, we turned this new Mach 5 into the fastest wheels in the business.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.660
It doesn't get any better than this.

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:57.860
You're telling me.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:11:59.820
Those are the stats.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.120
You think you can handle this baby?

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.010
Hmmm...

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:06.790
I'm asking you a question, son.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.510
You want me to drive the Mach 5?

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:11.510
No, I want my grandmother to drive the thing.

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:14.510
Yes, I want you to drive the Mach 5.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:17.400
How much more direct can I be? What do you want, a written invitation?

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:19.330
What do you say?

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:22.170
I never thought you'd trust me. So soon.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:25.810
Do it. And I'll do my best.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:29.740
I know you will, son. No one is more qualified to be behind that one.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:41.430
than you. The rest is history, Trixie. Five years ago, Rex pulled out of this garage, sped

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:52.970
down this track, and died on this very spot. Well, Rex, I fulfill part of my promise. I've

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:58.800
become a professional driver. And yet, I've got a long way to go before I can become half

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.780
the driver you were.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.710
This must be very hard for you.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.710
I didn't mean to bring all this up.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.010
We'll stop the interview.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:11.750
No.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.270
Did... did you actually see the accident?

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:24.760
Well, I was up in the tower, so it was hard to see much detail.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.100
I'm grateful for that.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.830
But I can still hear the roar of his engine.

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.000
I can still see...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.800
Smell the burning rubber. It's been many years, but it seems like it was yesterday.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:45.460
A track to myself. Terrific. Your brother and I are proud of you.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:49.240
Just keep your eyes on the road and everything will be just fine.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:59.830
Rex, what can I say, Dad? The Mach 5's a dream.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:04.640
For me, it was like a dream, to be there, to see my brother in the lead.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:08.950
My brother must be the greatest racer in the world.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:13.140
As long as he has the Mach 5, there isn't anything that can stop him.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.120
You could be right.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:21.680
Okay, Dad, I'm gonna finish this thing, in record time, if I can.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:27.300
As the Mach 5 accelerated, it became enveloped in a strange sheet of light.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.580
We got a problem!

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:37.570
what's happening to the systems what the devil rex didn't respond that strange sheet of light

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:53.720
grew bright do you copy me what the rex pull her over but he didn't answer and i've never felt so helpless

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:04.390
of light turned into a ball of blinding fire.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:34.230
I never found his body, or much of the car for that matter.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:37.330
That must have been awful.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:43.750
It was weird. I mean, no body, no helmet, nothing. He just completely vanished.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:50.760
And yet I can't believe that my brother's dead. I get this feeling that he's still there kind of watching over me.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:54.910
It's as if he's still alive. As if he could reappear tomorrow.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:59.410
Wow. Speed, I'm sorry.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.630
to bring up these memories.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.100
You'll have a heck of a news article.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:07.880
I don't think so, Speed.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.440
These memories are far too private

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:10.540
for me to be writing about.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.300
I won't publicize your loss.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:22.110
What's going on?

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:23.170
Is the place closed?

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:23.730
Hello?

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.110
There's my car.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:30.000
What the...

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:54.230
What do you think he's doing? Is he nuts?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.910
Go speed racer.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:05.020
Buy speed racer!

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:06.470
I know who this guy is!

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:09.130
The Silver Phantom!

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.910
Silver Phantom?

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:12.860
I heard a rumor about him in the newsroom.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:16.840
He's some kind of a nut who's bent on exterminating professional race drivers.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.680
Oh, come on!

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.840
You think I could make up something like this?

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.900
The guy is insane.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:25.400
He figures if he eliminates all the race drivers in the field,

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:28.640
he won't have much of a problem winning the final Grand Prix.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:35.090
Why didn't I think of that?

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:44.020
Now we'll see who's really the demon on wheels.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:46.520
Huh, it's the coppers.

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:49.950
Hungry boys?

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:51.000
Eat this!

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:10.820
this guy means business okay speed time to turn in for the night

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:48.190
- Yes!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.500
- I need to regret I asked for this interview.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.080
I mean, there are better ways of ditching a reporter.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.600
- What's the matter, he can't take a joke?

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:57.970
- It's not nice to turn your car into an airplane speed.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:00.000
That's bad sportsmanship.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.970
Stop, you lines of madness!

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:05.650
Hang on, Trix, here he comes.

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:09.670
Well, I've had just about enough of this guy's mad dance of terror.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:10.550
Activate!

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:11.900
Activate what?

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:22.440
Activate Cutter Blades!

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:28.580
Ah!

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:06.160
No brakes!

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:17.360
How's that for a professional driver?

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:21.500
The Mach 5's still in one piece.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:39.300
Speed Racer, with a little help from the Mach 5, assisted in the capture of the Silver Phantom.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:44.090
That's some scoop you got there, Trixie, but couldn't you have said a little more about the Mach 5?

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:47.090
I mean, after all, I put a lot of work into that thing!

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:48.470
Sorry, Sparky.

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:51.630
I cannot believe you rode in the Mach 5!

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:53.970
Do you have any idea how lucky you are?

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:57.650
Well, all in a day's work, Spridal. Isn't that right?

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.920
- Didn't even mention me. - Wha?

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:09.770
My dear Trixie, you hardly mention the car in your blurb, and the least you could do is mention the guy who's responsible for putting it together. Maybe next time, huh?

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:27.030
Look at him. It's past noon, and he's still fast asleep.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:30.000
I would be, too, if I went through the mill like he did.

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:32.920
He's some hero, that son of ours.

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:35.300
His brother would be proud.

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.780
No one could be prouder than I am.

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:42.000
Sleep well, Speed.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:46.260
Kept my promise, Rex.

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:49.490
I kept my promise.
